+
+## Complete Processing Example
+
+### Successful Case
+```
+CLI: frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+1. parseThresholds(['exact_match=0.9'])
+   → Regex match: ✓ 'exact_match' and '0.9'
+   → Parse float: 0.9 ✓
+   → Range check: 0 ≤ 0.9 ≤ 1 ✓
+   → Return: { thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9 }, errors: [] }
+
+2. validateThresholds({ exact_match: 0.9 }, evaluations)
+   → Metric 'exact_match' exists: ✓
+   → Return: []
+
+3. evaluateThresholds({ exact_match: 0.9 }, evaluations)
+   → score 0.95 >= min 0.9: ✓
+   → Return: { passed: true, thresholds: [{ metric, min, score, passed: true }] }
+
+4. generateReport(..., { exact_match: 0.9 })
+   → report.passed = true
+   → report.thresholds = [...]
+
+5. writeReport(report, 'json')
+   → report.json written
+
+6. Exit with code: 0 (success)
+```
+
+### Format Error Case
+```
+CLI: frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match
+
+1. parseThresholds(['exact_match'])
+   → Regex match: ✗ no '=' sign
+   → Return: { thresholds: undefined, errors: ["Invalid threshold format..."] }
+
+2. thresholdErrors.length > 0: ✓
+   → log.error("Invalid threshold format 'exact_match'. Expected format: <metric>=<number>")
+   → process.exit(2)
+
+Report NOT written
+Exit with code: 2 (usage error)
+```
+
+### Threshold Failure Case
+```
+CLI: frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.99
+
+1. parseThresholds(['exact_match=0.99']): ✓ Valid
+2. validateThresholds(...): ✓ Metric exists
+3. evaluateThresholds(...)
+   → score 0.95 < min 0.99: ✗
+   → Return: { passed: false, thresholds: [{ metric, min, score, passed: false }] }
+4. generateReport(..., ...)
+   → report.passed = false
+5. writeReport(report, 'json')
+   → report.json written with passed: false
+6. thresholds exist && !report.passed: ✓
+   → process.exit(1)
+
+Exit with code: 1 (evaluation failure)
+```
+
