+# Design Overview: `--threshold` Feature for `frai eval`
+
+## Executive Summary
+
+Adding `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option to the `frai eval` command requires changes in 2 files:
+
+1. **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`** - Add Thresholds section to markdown output
+2. **`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`** - Add CLI argument parsing and exit code handling
+
+**Total code changes: ~95 lines across 2 files**
+
+The core evaluation logic (`validateThresholds`, `evaluateThresholds`) is already implemented in frai-core.
+
+---
+
+## Feature Specification
+
+### Command Usage
+```bash
+# Single threshold
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --threshold toxicity=0.8
+
+# With report format
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --format markdown
+```
+
+### Available Metrics
+From `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`:
+- `exact_match`: Score 0-1, null if arrays mismatched
+- `toxicity`: Score 0-1, null if no outputs
+- `length_variance`: Score 0-1, null if arrays mismatched
+
+### Exit Codes
+- **0**: Success (all thresholds pass, or no thresholds specified)
+- **1**: Evaluation failure (threshold failed or score is null)
+- **2**: Usage error (malformed format, invalid range, unknown metric)
+
+### Validation Rules
+
+#### CLI-Level (parseThresholds)
+- Format: `<metric>=<number>` required
+- Range: 0 ≤ value ≤ 1 required
+- Examples:
+  - ✓ `exact_match=0.9`
+  - ✗ `exact_match` (missing =number)
+  - ✗ `exact_match=abc` (not a number)
+  - ✗ `exact_match=1.5` (out of range)
+
+#### Core-Level (validateThresholds)
+- Metric must exist in evaluations
+- Examples:
+  - ✓ `exact_match=0.9` (metric exists)
+  - ✗ `unknown_metric=0.9` (metric doesn't exist)
+
+#### Evaluation-Level (evaluateThresholds)
+- Score must be ≥ threshold
+- Null score = failure
+- Examples:
+  - ✓ score 0.95, threshold 0.9 → pass
+  - ✗ score 0.85, threshold 0.9 → fail
+  - ✗ score null, threshold 0.9 → fail
+
+### Report Output
+
+#### JSON Format
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": { ... },
+  "metrics": [ ... ],
+  "passed": true,
+  "thresholds": [
+    {
+      "metric": "exact_match",
+      "min": 0.9,
+      "score": 0.95,
+      "passed": true
+    },
+    {
+      "metric": "toxicity",
+      "min": 0.8,
+      "score": null,
+      "passed": false
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+#### Markdown Format
+```markdown
+## Thresholds
+
+| Metric | Min | Score | Result |
+|--------|-----|-------|--------|
+| exact_match | 0.90 | 0.95 | PASS |
+| toxicity | 0.80 | n/a | FAIL |
+```
+
+---
+
+## Architecture
+
+### Current State
+```
+frai-core/src/eval/index.js
+├── validateThresholds() ✓ Exists, exported
+├── evaluateThresholds() ✓ Exists, not directly exported
+└── generateReport()    ✓ Accepts thresholds param
+
+frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js
+├── toJson()            ✓ Works (JSON.stringify includes all fields)
+└── toMarkdown()        ✗ Missing Thresholds section
+
+frai-cli/src/index.ts
+├── eval command        ✗ No --threshold option
+└── runEvalCommand()    ✗ Doesn't process thresholds
+```
+
+### After Implementation
+```
+frai-core/src/eval/index.js
+├── validateThresholds() ✓ (no change)
+├── evaluateThresholds() ✓ (no change)
+└── generateReport()    ✓ (no change)
+
+frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js
+├── toJson()            ✓ (no change)
+└── toMarkdown()        ✓ NEW: Thresholds section
+
+frai-cli/src/index.ts
+├── EvalOptions         ✓ NEW: threshold?: string[]
+├── parseThresholds()   ✓ NEW: Format & range validation
+├── runEvalCommand()    ✓ MODIFIED: Full threshold support
+└── eval command        ✓ MODIFIED: --threshold option
+```
+
+---
+
+## Processing Flow
+
+### High-Level
+```
+CLI Input: frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+    ↓
+1. Parse CLI args → options.threshold = ['exact_match=0.9']
+    ↓
+2. parseThresholds() → { thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9 }, errors: [] }
+    ↓ (errors → exit 2)
+3. Load dataset and run evaluations
+    ↓
+4. validateThresholds() → Checks metric exists, returns errors
+    ↓ (errors → exit 2)
+5. generateReport(evaluations, thresholds)
+    → Calls evaluateThresholds() internally
+    → Adds passed and thresholds to report
+    ↓
+6. writeReport() → Outputs JSON or Markdown
+    ↓
+7. Exit with code based on report.passed
+    ↓ (thresholds exist and !passed → exit 1)
+    ↓ (success → exit 0)
+```
+
+### Error Handling Layers
+
+**Layer 1: CLI Format Validation** (parseThresholds)
+- Regex match `^([a-z_]+)=(.+)$`
+- Parse float
+- Check 0 ≤ value ≤ 1
+- Early exit 2 if invalid
+
+**Layer 2: Core Validation** (validateThresholds)
+- Check metric IDs exist in evaluations
+- Return list of errors
+- Exit 2 if errors found
+
+**Layer 3: Evaluation** (evaluateThresholds)
+- Compare score to threshold
+- Mark passed/failed
+- Exit 1 if any failed
+
+---
+
+## Code Changes Summary
+
+### Change 1: Markdown Thresholds Section
+**File:** `packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js` line 38  
+**Size:** ~15 lines  
+**Type:** Enhancement
+
+Add conditional section after metrics loop, before footer:
+```javascript
+if (report.thresholds && report.thresholds.length > 0) {
+  lines.push('## Thresholds');
+  lines.push('');
+  lines.push('| Metric | Min | Score | Result |');
+  lines.push('|--------|-----|-------|--------|');
+  report.thresholds.forEach((threshold) => {
+    const scoreDisplay = threshold.score !== null ? threshold.score : 'n/a';
+    const resultDisplay = threshold.passed ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL';
+    lines.push(`| ${threshold.metric} | ${threshold.min} | ${scoreDisplay} | ${resultDisplay} |`);
+  });
+  lines.push('');
+}
+```
+
+### Change 2: CLI Threshold Support
+**File:** `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`  
+**Size:** ~80 lines  
+**Type:** Feature (3 modifications)
+
+#### 2a. Update Type (line 51)
+Add to EvalOptions interface:
+```typescript
+threshold?: string[];
+```
+
+#### 2b. Add parseThresholds Function (before line 511)
+~35 lines parsing `metric=number` format, validating range
+
+#### 2c. Update runEvalCommand (lines 511-531)
+~40 lines handling:
+- parseThresholds with error handling
+- validateThresholds with error handling
+- Pass thresholds to generateReport
+- Exit code handling (0, 1, 2)
+
+#### 2d. Update eval command (line 773-784)
+Add option:
+```typescript
+.option('--threshold <metric>=<min>', 'Threshold for a metric (can be specified multiple times)')
+```
+
+---
+
+## Data Flow
+
+### Input → Processing → Output
+
+```
+options.threshold = ['exact_match=0.9', 'toxicity=0.8']
+    ↓ parseThresholds()
+{ exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.8 }
+    ↓ generateReport(evaluations, thresholds)
+report = {
+  metadata: {...},
+  metrics: [...],
+  passed: false,
+  thresholds: [
+    { metric: 'exact_match', min: 0.9, score: 0.95, passed: true },
+    { metric: 'toxicity', min: 0.8, score: null, passed: false }
+  ]
+}
+    ↓ writeReport(report, format)
+JSON: report.json (full structure)
+MD:   report.md (with Thresholds table)
+    ↓ process.exit(1)  // because passed: false
+Exit 1
+```
+
